# Reaction 36
reaction('O3 + HO2 <=> OH + O2 + O2', [6.620000e+09, 0.0, 994.0])
# !O3+NO=O2+NO2			8.43E+11 	0.00 	2603
# !O3+CO<=>O2+CO2			6.02E+02  0.00      0.00
# !O3+HCO<=>O2+H+CO2		5.00E+11  0.00      0.00
# !O3+CH3=CH3O+O2			5.83E+10 	0.00	 0
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# !The following reactiosn are from
# !Luther, K.; Oum, K.; Troe, J. Phys. Chem. Chem. Phys. 2005,7,2764-2770.
# ! and
# !Atkinson, R.; Baulch, D.L.; Cox, R.A.; Crowley, J.N.; Hampson, R.F.; Hynes, R.G.; Jenkin, M.E.; Rossi, M.J.; Troe, J.
# !Evaluated kinetic and photochemical data for atmospheric chemistry: Volume I - gas phase reactions of Ox, HOx, NOx and SOx species
# !Atmos. Chem. Phys.  4(2004) 1461 - 1738
# O2+O+AR=O3+AR  			4.29E+17 	-1.50 	0.
# duplicate
# O2+O+AR=O3+AR  			5.10E+21 	-3.20 	0.
# duplicate
# O2+O+HE=O3+HE  			5.16E+17 	-1.50 	0.
# duplicate
# O2+O+HE=O3+HE  			6.12E+21 	-3.20 	0.
# duplicate
# !put HE efficiency 20% higher than AR, it is usually true for most of reactions
# O2+O+M=O3+M 			6.53E+17 	-1.50 	0.
#    H2/2.0/ O2/0.95/ O3/2.5/ O/4.0/ AR/0.0/ HE/0.0/
# duplicate
# O2+O+M=O3+M 			1.33E+22 	-3.30 	0.
#    H2/2.0/ O2/1.07/ O3/2.5/ O/4.0/ AR/0.0/ HE/0.0/
# duplicate
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# !O3+O is taken from
# !Atkinson, R.; Baulch, D.L.; Cox, R.A.; Crowley, J.N.; Hampson, R.F.; Hynes, R.G.; Jenkin, M.E.; Rossi, M.J.; Troe, J.
# !Evaluated kinetic and photochemical data for atmospheric chemistry: Volume I - gas phase reactions of Ox, HOx, NOx and SOx species
# !Atmos. Chem. Phys.  4(2004) 1461 - 1738
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ! O3+O=O2(SING)+O2 is from
# !Vasiljeva, A. N.; Klopovskiy, K. S.; Kovalev, A. S.; Lopaev, D. V.; Mankelevich, Y. A.; Popov, N. A.; Rakhimov, A. T.; Rakhimova, T. V.
# !J. Phys. D: Appl. Phys.2004,37, 2455-2468.
# ! it is an estimate
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ! O3+H=O2+OH is taken from
# !DeMore, W.B.; Sander, S.P.; Golden, D.M.; Hampson, R.F.; Kurylo, M.J.; Howard, C.J.; Ravishankara, A.R.; Kolb, C.E.; Molina, M.J.
# !Chemical kinetics and photochemical data for use in stratospheric modeling. Evaluation number 12
# !JPL Publication 97-4  1997 1-266
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ! O3+H=O+HO2 is taken from
# !C.J. Howard, B.J. Finlayson-Pitts J. Chem. Phys., 72 (6) (1980), pp. 38423843
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ! O3+OH=O2+HO2 is from
# !A. Mansergas, J.M. Anglada  ChemPhysChem, 8 (2007), pp. 15341539
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# !O3+H2O=O2+H2O2 is from
# ! S. Hatakeyama, M.T. Leu J. Phys. Chem., 93 (1989), pp. 57845789
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ! O3+HO2=OH+O2+O2 is from
# !DeMore, W.B.; Sander, S.P.; Golden, D.M.; Hampson, R.F.; Kurylo, M.J.; Howard, C.J.; Ravishankara, A.R.; Kolb, C.E.; Molina, M.J.
# !Chemical kinetics and photochemical data for use in stratospheric modeling. Evaluation number 12
# !JPL Publication 97-4  1997 1-266
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ! the following two are from
# !R. Atkinson, D.L. Baulch, R.A. Cox, J.N. Crowley, R.F. Hampson, R.G. Hynes, M.E. Jenkin, M.J. Rossi, J. Troe
# ! Atmos. Chem. Phys., 4 (2004), pp. 14611738
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# !O3+CH3=CH3O+O2 is from
# !J. Albaladejo, E. Jimenez, A. Notario, B. Cabanas, E. Martinez
# !J. Phys. Chem. A, 106 (2002), pp. 25122519
